# EXPLORATORY DRAFT (LABS-1.021, Stage D review): profile organisation-0.1. Not installed.
# person and organisation are sortals (identity criteria differ from a generic physical/social object). Holding a role
# (an office) and having authority to act are kept apart: the office is a classification in a context; authority is a
# separate, attested conferral by a grantor, of a power, within a scope.
define
entity person sub physical-object;
entity organisation sub social-object;
relation employment sub proposition, relates employer, relates employee;
organisation plays employment:employer;
person plays employment:employee;
# single-holder offices: a subtype of classified-as, so a functional slot (class, context) -> classified can be
# declared for offices only, not for every classification
relation office-holding sub classified-as;
# authority: who conferred which power on whom, within what scope (an organisation, site or process)
relation authorisation sub proposition, relates grantor, relates holder, relates power, relates scope;
particular plays authorisation:grantor, plays authorisation:holder, plays authorisation:scope;
capability plays authorisation:power;
# an act performed in the capacity of an office (e.g. a sign-off as site manager)
relation decision sub event, relates decider as actor, relates capacity;
particular plays decision:decider;
social-role plays decision:capacity;
